Build option MESEN_NO_NETWORK: Mesen without its network code.

Mesen's library holds netplay (Core/Netplay, over Utilities/Socket) and
luasocket inside its Lua. With this option the Emulator makes no game server
or client, nothing asks whether netplay is connected (it never is), and the
Lua scripting context never offers socket.core or mime.core. The build then
leaves out Core/Netplay, Utilities/Socket.cpp and luasocket's sources
(waterbox/list-sources.py), so no network code is linked at all.

